# clang-tidy for the portable C, on the user's word of 14 October 2026
# (CLAUDE.md, "Strictness"): a broad set, the analyser, bugprone-* and
# misc-* and a few of readability-*, every check that is turned off with
# its reason above it, and every place that a check names an error. The
# test portable_c-tidy runs it over the common code and the files of
# Linux (harness/tidycheck.py). It is written for clang-tidy 23, which
# the test holds the version to: another version has other checks, which
# are judged before they are taken.
Checks:
  - "-*"
  - "clang-analyzer-*"
  - "bugprone-*"
  - "misc-*"
  - "readability-duplicate-include"
  - "readability-inconsistent-declaration-parameter-name"
  - "readability-misleading-indentation"
  - "readability-named-parameter"
  - "readability-redundant-declaration"
  - "readability-suspicious-call-argument"
  # A mask or a shift of a u8 or a u16, which C makes an int: the program
  # is written in such numbers by the rule of CLAUDE.md, "Numbers", and
  # every one of its masks would want a cast that says nothing, on the
  # user's word of 14 October 2026.
  - "-bugprone-signed-bitwise"
  # A switch without a default label, said twice, by this check and by
  # the next: a switch of the program does nothing for a value that it
  # has no case for, as the original's table of keys did nothing for a
  # key that it did not have, and a default that does nothing would say
  # so at a hundred places without saying anything.
  - "-bugprone-switch-missing-default-case"
  - "-bugprone-unhandled-code-paths"
  # Every file includes vc.h whole, by design: the headers are three, of
  # the program, of its tables and of the system, and a file is not to
  # name which declarations of them it uses.
  - "-misc-include-cleaner"
  # Two parameters of one type next to each other: the routines of the
  # original take a row and a column, a place and a length, and a
  # structure for each pair would be the layer's design, not a mend.
  - "-bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters"
  # A product reckoned in an int and then made a pointer's step, `screen
  # + 3 * 80`, `first + width * cursor`: the numbers are rows, columns
  # and entries, of 8 or 16 bits, whose product an int holds, which the
  # check cannot know; a cast to a wider type at each would say nothing.
  - "-bugprone-implicit-widening-of-multiplication-result"
  # A command of the main loop may go on into the loop again, as the
  # original's do: Command, CmdEnd, MnuEnd and F39_01 of main.c.
  - "-misc-no-recursion"
  # Two tests of a chain that do the same, as the original's do: in
  # F39_00 of menu.c a key held and a button of the mouse each choose a
  # table of commands, tested one after the other as the assembly tests
  # them, so that the code can be held against src/c and src/asm.
  - "-bugprone-branch-clone"
WarningsAsErrors: "*"
HeaderFilterRegex: "src/portable_c/.*"
